 "title": "A group of atoms behind a three-edge cut is an atom of the next level, reading as the AND of its atoms",
 "subject": "How grown atoms compose into levels, and what the level above reads of the one below",
 "conclusion": "A knot sphere with a flat state at every line, carrying atoms that each act in exactly one class and are free, is again such an atom: less any point it acts as its replaced line exactly where every atom inside acts, at any depth, and a composite of genus g holds g - 1 units, g where it acts (proved by hand). Computed: the AND at 274 removed points, 576 classes exact, 11 of 12 two-level addresses held.",
